IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- The 2026 Florida Statutes, chapter 414 (Family Self-Sufficiency) -- temporary cash assistance (TCA), Florida's TANF cash
-- programme: resources (s 414.075); income eligibility (s 414.085); eligibility, the three-tier payment standard, the
-- disregards and the calculation (s 414.095(2), (5), (6), (7), (8), (10), (11), (12), (14)); and the 48-month limit and its
-- exemptions (s 414.105).
--
-- SEAT: the applicant (the parent or caretaker relative). "Does my family qualify? How much would we get each month? How
-- long can we get it? What must I report, and by when?" The Department of Children and Families appears only as what it must
-- or may do to the family.
--
-- Edition: The 2026 Florida Statutes (Online Sunshine, www.leg.state.fl.us), chapter 414, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/fla-stat-ch414.txt (retrieved 2026-10-19). The Legislature's editorial notes are not in the
-- deposit.
--
-- INPUTS, not in the deposited statute: the federal poverty level for the family (s 414.085(1)(a) ties the gross income limit
-- to 185% of it). The DCF ESS Program Policy Manual Appendix A-5 (deposited in the sibling subject
-- ../../../florida-dcf-ess-program-policy-manual-appendix-a-5-and-a-12-cash-assistance-and-oss-standards/) prints 185% of FPL
-- "effective April 2026"; it is a policy-manual appendix, not a rule, so its figures appear here only as a default the person
-- can override (NOTES.md finding 2).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: work requirements and sanctions (s 414.065, ch. 445); drug screening (s 414.0652); the family cap
-- (s 414.115); the federal food assistance definitions borrowed by ss 414.075 and 414.085 (7 C.F.R. ss 273.8, 273.9: whether
-- an item is a resource or income is asked as a fact); noncitizen rules beyond the citizenship question (s 414.095(3)); teen
-- parents (s 414.095(14)(b), (c)); the proportional reduction (s 414.095(16), a funding decision); fraud and overpayments.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the applicant's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Florida temporary cash assistance`

§§ `Questions this encoding does not cover`

DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    `the s 414.095(10) chart stops at a family of 13`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH A TYPE
DECLARE `Answer` a IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `the answer` IS AN a
    `not covered` HAS `because`    IS A `Why not covered`

§§ `s 414.095(10) -- the three-tier shelter payment standard`

-- (10): "There shall be three assistance levels for a family that contains a specified number of eligible members, based on
-- the following criteria: (a) A family that does not have a shelter obligation. (b) A family that has a shelter obligation
-- greater than zero but less than or equal to $50. (c) A family that has a shelter obligation greater than $50 or that is
-- homeless." The chart: Family Size | Zero | Greater than Zero Less than or Equal to $50 | Greater than $50.
DECLARE `Shelter obligation` IS ONE OF
    `no shelter obligation`
    `a shelter obligation over $0 and not over $50`
    `a shelter obligation over $50, or homeless`

DECLARE `Payment standards` HAS
    `zero`             IS A NUMBER
    `up to 50`         IS A NUMBER
    `over 50`          IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the family size` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Answer` `Payment standards`
`the s 414.095(10) chart row for` `the family size` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the family size` AT MOST 1  THEN `answered` (`Payment standards` OF 95, 153, 180)
        IF `the family size` EQUALS 2   THEN `answered` (`Payment standards` OF 158, 205, 241)
        IF `the family size` EQUALS 3   THEN `answered` (`Payment standards` OF 198, 258, 303)
        IF `the family size` EQUALS 4   THEN `answered` (`Payment standards` OF 254, 309, 364)
        IF `the family size` EQUALS 5   THEN `answered` (`Payment standards` OF 289, 362, 426)
        IF `the family size` EQUALS 6   THEN `answered` (`Payment standards` OF 346, 414, 487)
        IF `the family size` EQUALS 7   THEN `answered` (`Payment standards` OF 392, 467, 549)
        IF `the family size` EQUALS 8   THEN `answered` (`Payment standards` OF 438, 519, 610)
        IF `the family size` EQUALS 9   THEN `answered` (`Payment standards` OF 485, 570, 671)
        IF `the family size` EQUALS 10  THEN `answered` (`Payment standards` OF 534, 623, 733)
        IF `the family size` EQUALS 11  THEN `answered` (`Payment standards` OF 582, 676, 795)
        IF `the family size` EQUALS 12  THEN `answered` (`Payment standards` OF 630, 728, 857)
        IF `the family size` EQUALS 13  THEN `answered` (`Payment standards` OF 678, 781, 919)
        OTHERWISE `not covered` `the s 414.095(10) chart stops at a family of 13`

GIVEN `the row` IS A `Payment standards`
      `the shelter obligation` IS A `Shelter obligation`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the payment standard in` `the row` `for` `the shelter obligation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the shelter obligation`
    WHEN `no shelter obligation`                         THEN `the row`'s `zero`
    WHEN `a shelter obligation over $0 and not over $50` THEN `the row`'s `up to 50`
    WHEN `a shelter obligation over $50, or homeless`    THEN `the row`'s `over 50`

§§ `The family's month`

DECLARE `TCA family` HAS
    `family size`                                       IS A NUMBER
    `shelter obligation`                                IS A `Shelter obligation`
    `a current participant`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `earned income of adults`                           IS A NUMBER
    `earned income of children in high school, 19 or younger` IS A NUMBER  -- s 414.095(11)(b)
    `unearned income counted`                           IS A NUMBER  -- after the s 414.085(1)(b) exclusions (SSI and the like)
    `child support received`                            IS A NUMBER  -- s 414.085(1)(c): not disregarded
    `resources counted`                                 IS A NUMBER  -- after the s 414.075(2) exclusions
    `185 percent of the federal poverty level for the family` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `f` IS A `TCA family`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the gross family income of` `f` MEANS
        `f`'s `earned income of adults`
    PLUS `f`'s `earned income of children in high school, 19 or younger`
    PLUS `f`'s `unearned income counted`
    PLUS `f`'s `child support received`

-- s 414.085(1)(a): "Participation in the temporary cash assistance program shall be limited to those families whose gross
-- family income is equal to or less than 185 percent of the federal poverty level". The child's earnings disregard of
-- s 414.095(11)(b) is read as reaching this test too ("A child's earned income shall be disregarded"; NOTES.md finding 4).
GIVEN `f` IS A `TCA family`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the family passes the 185 percent test` IF
    (`the gross family income of` `f` MINUS `f`'s `earned income of children in high school, 19 or younger`)
        AT MOST `f`'s `185 percent of the federal poverty level for the family`

-- s 414.075(1): "The maximum allowable resources, including liquid and nonliquid resources, of all members of the family may not
-- exceed $2,000." (2)(a): licensed vehicles needed for work, training or education up to a combined $8,500 are excluded (asked
-- in the counted figure).
GIVEN `f` IS A `TCA family`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the family's resources are within the limit` IF
    `f`'s `resources counted` AT MOST 2000

§§ `s 414.095(11), (12) -- the disregards and the amount`

-- (11)(a): "As an incentive to employment, the first $200 plus one-half of the remainder of earned income shall be disregarded.
-- In order to be eligible for earned income to be disregarded, the individual must be: 1. A current participant in the program;
-- or 2. Eligible for participation in the program without the earnings disregard." "Eligible without the disregard" is read as:
-- income counted without it leaves something to pay under the payment standard (NOTES.md finding 3).
-- (11)(b): "A child's earned income shall be disregarded if the child is a family member, attends high school or the
-- equivalent, and is 19 years of age or younger."
-- (12)(a): "Temporary cash assistance shall be calculated based on average monthly gross family income, earned and unearned,
-- less any applicable disregards. The resulting monthly net income amount shall be subtracted from the applicable payment
-- standard". (b): "A deduction may not be allowed for child care payments."
GIVEN `the earned income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the $200 and one-half disregard of` `the earned income` MEANS
    min `the earned income` (200 PLUS (max 0 (`the earned income` MINUS 200)) DIVIDED BY 2)

GIVEN `f` IS A `TCA family`
      `the standard` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the net income of` `f` `against the standard` `the standard` MEANS
    IF   `gets the (11)(a) disregard`
    THEN `without the (11)(a) disregard` MINUS `the $200 and one-half disregard of` (`f`'s `earned income of adults`)
    ELSE `without the (11)(a) disregard`
    WHERE
        `without the (11)(a) disregard` MEANS
                `f`'s `earned income of adults` PLUS `f`'s `unearned income counted` PLUS `f`'s `child support received`
        `gets the (11)(a) disregard` MEANS
            `f`'s `a current participant` OR `without the (11)(a) disregard` LESS THAN `the standard`

GIVEN `f` IS A `TCA family`
      `the standard` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the monthly TCA for` `f` `with payment standard` `the standard` MEANS
    IF   `the family passes the 185 percent test` `f` AND `the family's resources are within the limit` `f`
    THEN max 0 (`the standard` MINUS `the net income of` `f` `against the standard` `the standard`)
    ELSE 0

§§ `s 414.095(2), (5), (6), (7), (14) -- the other conditions`

DECLARE `TCA conditions` HAS
    `a US citizen or qualified noncitizen`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `a legal resident of Florida`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `every member has given a social security number or proof of applying` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a minor child lives in the home with a parent or relative caretaker` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a pregnant woman in the ninth month, or in the last trimester and restricted from work by a physician` IS A BOOLEAN
    `cooperates with child support enforcement, or has good cause` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has assigned support rights to the Department of Revenue` IS A BOOLEAN
    `fleeing prosecution, custody or confinement, or violating probation or parole` IS A BOOLEAN
    `convicted of receiving benefits in two or more states at once within the last 10 years` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (2)(a)1.-5., (5), (6), (7), (14)(a), (d) to (g).
GIVEN `c` IS A `TCA conditions`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the other conditions are met` IF
        `c`'s `a US citizen or qualified noncitizen`
    AND `c`'s `a legal resident of Florida`
    AND `c`'s `every member has given a social security number or proof of applying`
    AND (    `c`'s `a minor child lives in the home with a parent or relative caretaker`
         OR  `c`'s `a pregnant woman in the ninth month, or in the last trimester and restricted from work by a physician`)
    AND `c`'s `cooperates with child support enforcement, or has good cause`
    AND `c`'s `has assigned support rights to the Department of Revenue`
    AND (NOT `c`'s `fleeing prosecution, custody or confinement, or violating probation or parole`)
    AND (NOT `c`'s `convicted of receiving benefits in two or more states at once within the last 10 years`)

§§ `s 414.105 -- the 48-month limit`

-- s 414.105: "an applicant or current participant shall receive temporary cash assistance for no more than a lifetime cumulative
-- total of 48 months, unless otherwise provided by law." (4): months of TANF in another state count. (7): "Child-only cases are
-- not subject to time limitations, and temporary cash assistance received while an individual is a minor child shall not count".
-- (8): SSI or SSDI recipients are not subject to it, and an applicant for SSI or SSDI "must be granted an extension ... until
-- ... a final determination". (9): a person "totally responsible for the personal care of a disabled family member" with no
-- alternative care is not subject to it. (1), (2): hardship exemptions (the department's judgment, capped at 20% of the
-- caseload), including for victims of domestic violence.
DECLARE `What the 48-month limit means for me` IS ONE OF
    `the 48-month limit does not apply to me (s 414.105(7), (8) or (9))`
    `I must be granted an extension until my SSI or SSDI application is finally decided (s 414.105(8))`
    `I am within the 48 months`
    `I have reached 48 months: TCA continues only with a hardship exemption (s 414.105(1), (2))`

DECLARE `Time limit facts` HAS
    `a child-only case`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `receives SSI or SSDI`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `has applied for SSI or SSDI and awaits a final determination` IS A BOOLEAN
    `totally responsible for the care of a disabled family member, with no alternative care` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months of TCA or other states' TANF received as an adult` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `t` IS A `Time limit facts`
GIVETH A `What the 48-month limit means for me`
`the s 414.105 answer for` `t` MEANS
    IF   `t`'s `a child-only case` OR `t`'s `receives SSI or SSDI`
         OR `t`'s `totally responsible for the care of a disabled family member, with no alternative care`
    THEN `the 48-month limit does not apply to me (s 414.105(7), (8) or (9))`
    ELSE IF   `t`'s `months of TCA or other states' TANF received as an adult` LESS THAN 48
         THEN `I am within the 48 months`
         ELSE IF   `t`'s `has applied for SSI or SSDI and awaits a final determination`
              THEN `I must be granted an extension until my SSI or SSDI application is finally decided (s 414.105(8))`
              ELSE `I have reached 48 months: TCA continues only with a hardship exemption (s 414.105(1), (2))`

§§ `Duties and dates`

DECLARE `TCA party` IS ONE OF
    `the parent or caretaker relative`
    `the applicant`

DECLARE `TCA action` IS ONE OF
    `report the child's absence to the department`
    `respond to the scheduled appointments or contact the department`

-- s 414.095(14)(h): "The parent or other caretaker relative must report to the department by the end of the 5-day period that
-- begins on the date it becomes clear to the parent or caretaker relative that a minor child will be absent from the home for
-- 30 or more consecutive days. A parent or caretaker relative who fails to report this information to the department shall be
-- disqualified from receiving temporary cash assistance for 30 days for the first occurrence, 60 days for the second
-- occurrence, and 90 days for the third or subsequent occurrence." Day 0 is the first of the five days.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `TCA party` `TCA action`
`the 5 days to report a child's absence` MEANS
    PARTY  `the parent or caretaker relative`
    MUST   `report the child's absence to the department`
    WITHIN 4
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `the parent or caretaker relative` BECAUSE "a child's absence of 30 or more days not reported by the end of the 5-day period: disqualified from TCA for 30 days (first), 60 days (second) or 90 days (third or later) (s 414.095(14)(h))"

GIVEN `earlier failures to report` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days of disqualification after failure number` `earlier failures to report` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `earlier failures to report` AT MOST 0 THEN 30
        IF `earlier failures to report` EQUALS 1  THEN 60
        OTHERWISE                                     90

-- s 414.095(8): "The request shall be denied 30 days after the initial application if the applicant fails to respond to
-- scheduled appointments, including appointments with the state agency responsible for administering the child support
-- enforcement program, and does not contact the department or authorized entity regarding the application." (a): "The
-- beginning date of eligibility for temporary cash assistance is the date on which the application is approved or 30 days
-- after the date of application, whichever is earlier."
GIVETH A DEONTIC `TCA party` `TCA action`
`the 30 days to keep the application alive` MEANS
    PARTY  `the applicant`
    MUST   `respond to the scheduled appointments or contact the department`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "no response to scheduled appointments and no contact within 30 days: the request is denied (s 414.095(8))"

GIVEN `the date of application` IS A DATE
      `the date of approval` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the beginning date of eligibility for` `the date of application` `approved on` `the date of approval` MEANS
    IF   `the date of approval` LESS THAN (`the date of application` PLUS 30)
    THEN `the date of approval`
    ELSE `the date of application` PLUS 30

§ `Questions for the applicant`

§§ `How much?`

@export What are Florida's TCA payment standards for a family of this size, by shelter obligation (s 414.095(10))?
GIVEN `my family size` IS A NUMBER @desc How many eligible members are in your family (1 to 13)
GIVETH AN `Answer` `Payment standards`
`What are the TCA payment standards for my family` MEANS `the s 414.095(10) chart row for` `my family size`

@export How much temporary cash assistance would my family get each month (s 414.095(12))?
GIVEN `my family size` IS A NUMBER @desc How many eligible members are in your family (1 to 13)
      `our shelter obligation` IS A `Shelter obligation` @desc Your family's monthly shelter obligation: none, over $0 up to $50, or over $50 (or homeless)
      `we are already receiving TCA` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a current participant in the program
      `adults' earnings this month` IS A NUMBER @desc Average monthly gross earnings of the adults, in US dollars
      `earnings of children in high school` IS A NUMBER @desc Earnings of family members who attend high school or the equivalent and are 19 or younger, in US dollars
      `other income this month` IS A NUMBER @desc Unearned income that counts (not SSI or other income security payments), in US dollars
      `child support this month` IS A NUMBER @desc Child support received this month, in US dollars (all of it counts)
      `our resources` IS A NUMBER @desc Your family's countable resources (not counting vehicles up to $8,500 needed for work, training or school), in US dollars
      `185 percent of the poverty level for my family` IS A NUMBER @desc 185% of the federal poverty level for your family's size, monthly, in US dollars (DCF's Appendix A-5 for April 2026 prints $4,212 for a family of 3)
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`How much TCA would we get` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the s 414.095(10) chart row for` `my family size`
    WHEN `not covered` `the gap` THEN `not covered` `the gap`
    WHEN `answered` `the row` THEN
        `answered` (`the monthly TCA for`
                        (`TCA family` OF `my family size`, `our shelter obligation`, `we are already receiving TCA`, `adults' earnings this month`,
                                        `earnings of children in high school`, `other income this month`, `child support this month`,
                                        `our resources`, `185 percent of the poverty level for my family`)
                        `with payment standard` (`the payment standard in` `the row` `for` `our shelter obligation`))

@export Does my family meet the other conditions for TCA: citizenship, residence, a child at home, child support and the bars in s 414.095?
GIVEN `I am a citizen or qualified noncitizen` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the applicant is a US citizen or a qualified noncitizen (refugee, asylee, permanent resident and the others listed in s 414.095(3))
      `we live in Florida` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the applicant is a legal resident of Florida
      `everyone has a social security number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every family member has given a social security number or proof of applying for one
      `a minor child lives with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a minor child lives in the home with you as parent or relative caretaker
      `I am pregnant and in the last month, or last trimester on doctor's orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If there is no child: whether you are a pregnant woman in the ninth month, or in the last trimester and restricted from work by a physician
      `I cooperate on child support` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you cooperate with child support enforcement (identifying the other parent, paternity, support orders), or have good cause not to
      `I have assigned support rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have assigned your family's rights to support to the Department of Revenue
      `someone is a fleeing felon or violating parole` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the applicant is fleeing prosecution, custody or confinement for a felony, or violating probation or parole
      `someone was convicted of getting benefits in two states at once` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the applicant was convicted, in the last 10 years, of receiving these benefits in two or more states at the same time
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my family meet the other TCA conditions` IF
    `the other conditions are met`
        (`TCA conditions` OF `I am a citizen or qualified noncitizen`, `we live in Florida`, `everyone has a social security number`,
                            `a minor child lives with me`, `I am pregnant and in the last month, or last trimester on doctor's orders`,
                            `I cooperate on child support`, `I have assigned support rights`, `someone is a fleeing felon or violating parole`,
                            `someone was convicted of getting benefits in two states at once`)

@export How does the 48-month lifetime limit on TCA apply to me (s 414.105)?
GIVEN `this is a child-only case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether only the children receive TCA (no adult is included)
      `I receive SSI or SSDI` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you receive Supplemental Security Income or Social Security Disability Insurance
      `I am waiting for an SSI or SSDI decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have applied for SSI or SSDI and are waiting for a final determination (including appeals)
      `I care full time for a disabled family member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are totally responsible for the personal care of a disabled family member and no alternative care is available
      `months of TCA I have had as an adult` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months of TCA (or of TANF in other states) you have received as an adult
GIVETH A `What the 48-month limit means for me`
`How does the 48-month limit apply to me` MEANS
    `the s 414.105 answer for`
        (`Time limit facts` OF `this is a child-only case`, `I receive SSI or SSDI`, `I am waiting for an SSI or SSDI decision`,
                              `I care full time for a disabled family member`, `months of TCA I have had as an adult`)

§§ `Dates`

@export From what date does my family's TCA eligibility begin (s 414.095(8)(a))?
GIVEN `the date of my application` IS A DATE @desc The date the department received your signed and dated request to participate
      `the date it was approved` IS A DATE @desc The date your application was approved
GIVETH A DATE
`From when does our TCA begin` MEANS `the beginning date of eligibility for` `the date of my application` `approved on` `the date it was approved`

@export By what date must I report that my child will be away from home for 30 days or more (s 414.095(14)(h))?
GIVEN `the day it became clear` IS A DATE @desc The day it became clear to you that your child will be absent from the home for 30 or more consecutive days
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I report my child's absence` MEANS `the day it became clear` PLUS 4

@export If I do not report my child's absence in time, for how many days am I disqualified from TCA (s 414.095(14)(h))?
GIVEN `earlier failures` IS A NUMBER @desc How many times before you have failed to report a child's absence in time
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How long am I disqualified for not reporting` MEANS `the days of disqualification after failure number` `earlier failures`
